  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "A person measures the depth of a well by measuring the time interval between dropping a stone and receiving the sound of impact with the bottom of the well. The error in his measurement of time is <math><mi>&#948;</mi><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.01</mn></math> seconds and he measures the depth of the well to be L = 20 meters. Take the acceleration due to gravity <math><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>m</mi><msup><mrow><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> and the velocity of sound is <math><mn>300</mn><mi>m</mi><msup><mrow><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> . Then the fractional error in the measurement, <math><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#948;</mi><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow></mfrac></math> , is closest to",
    "image": null
  },
